      "text": "Pattonsburg relocated four miles north of its original site after the Great Flood of 1993 devastated the old town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattonsburg%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The new town sits on higher ground, a decision made by residents to escape future flood damage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattonsburg%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Big Creek runs just east of Pattonsburg, joining the Grand River about two miles southeast of the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
